ailure transition on the\n24:   device path until the timeout). F\u002dRS\u002d08 and F\u002dRS\u002d09 High (the phone page drops pre\u002dtyped text; Back bypasses the\n25:   box). F\u002dRS\u002d11 High pending a fact: `wait` returns at success under the bridge's grab, the exact ordering the\n26:   code's own comments say leaves ES without a pad; both halves were written in `e4597faf23` and the VM has no\n27:   gamepad, so nothing has ever seen it either way \u002d\u002d a uinput gamepad on the guest is the proof to write.\n28: \u002d **Bucket 8's GPT seat.** Three buffered attempts on the 1 MB EmulationStation packet ended `http=200 content=0b\n29:   response_body_error` (615, 888 and 320 s); `\u002d\u002dtransport sse` is refused for that seat (only the Foundry and\n30:   Bedrock recipes stream). Split by path into `8a\u002des\u002dapp` (464 KB) and `8b\u002des\u002dcore` (556 KB), each with its own\n31:   manifest and a brief that says the other half is outside the packet; both dispatched. The Claude seat's\n32:   single\u002dpacket output stands. 16 of 20 seat outputs in at 23:48.\n33: \u002d **The staging scripts for `7911c53bb4`** (`stage\u002drg35xxsp\u002d7911c53bb4.sh`, `stage\u002dand\u002dreboot\u002d7911c53bb4.sh`)\n34:   are written from the last cut's with the label in double quotes and refuse to run (rc 4, proven) until the\n35:   maintainer's words replace `YES_QUOTE_NOT_GIVEN`; the copy and the reboot are each theirs to say (D\u002dQA\u002d011).\n\nTARGET 67 docs/work\u002dlogs/2026_09\u002dwork_logs/2026_09_28\u002dwork_log.md bounded\u002dday\u002dentry\nIDENTITY 6ed68c9d076835f2067091b4357b4dc29b307b87 34e808171e5219989ceff721390c85dcd56f316f2b1d2a24bbe1a290c98bc556 RANGES [[205, 208]] MASKED []\n205: ## 23:55 UTC \u2014 #315 fixed in the scripts (`286759eb6d`): the harness PASSED 1232, section S315 seen to fail on the unfixed scripts\n206: \n207: `remote_compares_by_size` in both cloud scripts (the same text, read from `rclone.conf`); `\u002d