le, three quarters under 85, the largest 3,046; the map's header now carries a ceiling of 1,500 insertions and 30 files, and `tools/pr\u002dstack\u002dcheck` fails five of the ten PRs against it. Upstream's own tree carries 277 in\u002dtree kernel patches, so the file's kernel rule is read as written for agents, not for a device's reservation patch. Prong 1 of #335 is the primary path again, at the project's pace: about twenty distribution PRs and fifteen interface PRs after the move out of `GuiMenu.cpp`, one at a time.\n\nTARGET 69 docs/work\u002dlogs/2026_09\u002dwork_logs/2026_09_30\u002dwork_log.md bounded\u002dday\u002dentry\nIDENTITY f8a82ff4f4cc889783218238254598626d6addc5 039135dcee3ed5810125d710569a68927ecb28005c9d3d16ba244fd04e01c193 RANGES [[141, 144]] MASKED []\n141: ## 23:54 UTC \u2014 D\u002dCLOUD\u002d157 and D\u002dCLOUD\u002d158: the cloud changes ship in 0.0.1 as the epic #354; the default cloud folder becomes /Rasteratops (milestone \"rasteratops 0.0.1\", #7)\n142: \n143: The maintainer's call after the Nova's evening: the cloud fixes go into the next candidate and 0.0.1 (*\"release candidate 3 slash 4 version 0.0.1\"*), everything looks for `/Rasteratops`, the guards go in, and the scan\u002dfirst flow is resolved for this initial version; all bundled into one epic. Done: the milestone with its acceptance test, the epic #354 with #349 #350 #351 #352 #353 as sub\u002dissues (and #344, #337 under the milestone), the two rows (157 reverses #344's \"outside 0.0.1\" for the folder; 158 reverses D\u002dWORKFLOW\u002d101's \"unchanged\", keeping its mixed\u002dinstallation gate), #344's body line struck with the rows cited and a comment, and the old\u002dwords sweep as a checkbox on #353 (the row's rule). Owed by the ceremonies: a futro for the new epic within three days (`ceremonies.md`).\n\nTARGET 70 docs/work\u002dlogs/2026_10\u002dwork_logs/2026_10_01\u002dwork_log.md bounded\u002dday\u002dentry\nIDENTITY 4b4582da3de8ea9d7de067e2ebefca4540cbc53e 46c8bc353356cbd095df45cd68fbccd9c350ad5c1b41b5588a143c3bcd5eb8d2 RANGES [[325, 367]] MASKED []\n325: ## 23:27 UTC \u2014 #363, D\u002dCLOUD\u002d170: the cloud folder step replaces the check before every sync\n326: \n327: \u002d **What changed.** `cloud_backup` and `cloud_restore` no longer run\n328:   `cloud_migrate_layout \u002d\u002dfollow` before a sync. The folder is settled by a\n329:   step: at the end of cloud setup, before the seeding and CLOUD SETUP COMPLETE\n330:   (`cloud_scan \u002d\u002dfolder`, then MOVE / KEEP USING / NOT NOW when an earlier\n331:   folder holds saves), and at boot for a conf on an earlier default not kept\n332:   with a remote set up (`cloud_migrate_layout \u002d\u002dneeds\u002dstep`, no network), once\n333:   the startup sync has ended and the screen is free. Offline at boot it asks\n334:   FINISH CLOUD SETUP with CONNECT TO WI\u002dFI and NOT NOW. FINISH RESTORE PROCESS\n335:   comes first; its FINISH arms the step. ES `e108699ea`.\n336: \u002d **Why a waiter and not a page at boot.** The step needs the startup sync to\n337:   have ended (a move takes the lock the sync holds; asked beside it, the move\n338:   was refused as A SYNC IS ALREADY RUNNING) and the screen free (not over a\n339:   menu the player opened meanwhile, not during a game). A detached thread asks\n340:   `\u002d\u002dneeds\u002dstep`, waits for the sync, gives a link coming up its time\n341:   (`cloud_net_ready \u002d\u002dwait 30`), then posts a check once a second through\n342:   `AppWindow::post`, one post in flight at a time. FINISH on the restore page\n343:   arms the same waiter rather than opening the step at once.\n344: \u002d **What the trade costs.** A handheld already on that writes into the old\n345:   folder after another device moved it is no longer followed before that\n346:   write; its next step reads the move with the fleet's folder there and MOVE\n347:   merges (D\u002dCLOUD\u002d168). The pair test's step 5m stages exactly that.\n348: \u002d **The transfer page's new hook.** `GuiCloudTransfer::setDismissedAction`:\n349:   what a page closed without its completed action goes on to, so a scan or a\n350:   move that fails at the end of setup still reaches the setup's last page.\n351: \u002d **The online test is the scan's own** (a default route), so the step and its\n352:   scan never disagree about offline. **`\u002d\u002dneeds\u002dstep` compares names as\n353:   written**: with no network it cannot ask whether the cloud folds case, and a\n354:   hand\u002dtyped lowercase folder a case\u002dsensitive cloud calls the player's own\n355:   would otherwise put a scan up at every boot.\n356: \u002d **The forks taken inside the decision** are a row of their own, D\u002dCLOUD\u002d171:\n357:   only the move asked at setup, the boot step's wait for a free screen (and\n358:   FINISH arming the same wait), offline as no default route, and names\n359:   compared as written.\n360: \u002d **#363's body** was rewritten around the decision (its first proposal kept,\n361:   marked superseded) with ten checkboxes naming their artifacts; box\u002dcheck is\n362:   clean again (the old wording named \"a device\" with no physical fact).\n363: \u002d **The suite**: the working tree PASSED whole (`lgst\u002dstep.log`, 23:22\u002d23:29);\n364:   against HEAD, `\u002d\u002dold`, exactly the 13 new cases FAIL \u002d\u002d six `\u002d\u002dneeds\u002dstep`\n365:   answers, the two sync scripts' missing check, five of `cloud_scan\n366:   \u002d\u002dfolder`'s (`lgst\u002dstep\u002dold.log`, 23:29\u002d23:36).\n\nTARGET 71 docs/work\u002dlogs/2026_10\u002dwork_logs/2026_10_02\u002dwork_log.md bounded\u002dday\u002dentry\nIDENTITY 6c8a6dd995223d21a72c176ac0bdf55312d7ad37 3dcb61185933011af7a786a44302a443d0ee2fe9b4abc149535b48359702f530 RANGES [[685, 707]] MASKED []\n685: ## 23:08 UTC \u2014 #388: milestone body is the execution queue; naming restored\n686: \n687: The maintainer asked that the current priorities live in the GitHub milest